**The Risk Cards:**

Issues are displayed as expandable accordion cards, sorted by severity.

**🔴 Critical (Red Card):**
```
CRITICAL — Array of Objects Cannot Be Stored in a Single Column
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The "orders" collection has an "items" field which is an array of
objects. This cannot be stored directly as a column in PostgreSQL.

→ Suggested Fix: Create a separate "order_items" table with a
  foreign key referencing orders.id (already applied in your mapping).

[Mark as Acknowledged]   [Go Back to Fix Mapping]
```

**🟡 Warning (Amber Card):**
```
